<edge source="us_china_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="ai_buildout_risks::capability_growth_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls restrict access to advanced GPUs, AI accelerators and pre‑trained model weights for targeted actors, directly slowing their ability to train larger models and thereby reducing model capability growth rates.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_risks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="ai_buildout_risks::infra_financing_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Broad sanctions and export restrictions raise compliance and sanctions‑risk for banks, investors and cloud providers, causing them to withdraw, delay, or redirect capital away from affected AI infrastructure projects.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_risks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="global_bond_repricing::long_term_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid ramp‑up in export controls on critical technologies raises persistent geopolitical and supply‑risk perceptions, increasing term premiums as investors demand compensation for higher long‑run growth and earnings uncertainty, which lifts long‑dated sovereign yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_rivalry::export_control_intensity" target="iran_gulf_conflict::oil_price_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter U.S. export controls on advanced technologies raise market perceptions of an elevated risk of broader Sino‑U.S. escalation (including spillover to Gulf security), causing traders and refiners to widen risk premia and increase short‑term oil price volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
