  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in oil-price volatility raise market participants' expected future energy costs and pass-through risk to consumer prices, causing market and survey-based inflation expectations to rise rapidly.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
