<edge source="global_bond_repricing::long_term_yield" target="ai_buildout_risks::infra_financing_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising long-term sovereign yields raise discount rates and borrowing costs for long‑duration projects, which directly reduces bank lending and investor appetite for large, capital‑intensive data centers and cloud buildouts, lowering net financing flows into AI infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_risks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::long_term_yield" target="russia_ukraine_security::escalation_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in global long-term yields increases borrowing costs and fiscal strain for Western donor governments, making sustained high-level military support for Ukraine politically and financially harder and thereby causing Russian decision‑makers to perceive a greater window to escalate.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_security</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::long_term_yield" target="us_china_rivalry::corporate_engagement" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising long‑term sovereign yields increase the cost of capital and lower valuations for multi‑year projects, causing multinational firms to scale back investment, joint ventures, and high‑visibility engagement in China, reducing corporate diplomatic interaction.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
